# gitleaks baseline (#483): fingerprints of KNOWN, REVIEWED false positives.
# One exact finding per line, ALWAYS commit-pinned (commit:file:rule:line).
# Never add a bare file:rule:line entry: it would also apply to the pre-commit
# staged scan, so a real key written at that same line would be silently
# ignored. A commit-pinned entry cannot match new content (a new commit has a
# new SHA). The pre-commit scan only sees staged added lines, and the CI scan
# only the commits a PR adds, so untouched fixtures are never reported there.
# Reviewed 2026-10-13: every entry is a fake test value or a documentation
# placeholder, no real secret.
#
# - 2410702 logging/redaction *.spec.ts (generic-api-key): fixed fake token
#   the tests assert is masked in logs and Sentry events.
# - 396822b env.validation.spec.ts: JWT_SECRET placeholder (generic-api-key)
#   and a truncated "-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n..." hint (private-key, no
#   key material).
# - 396822b wdsf.service.spec.ts (generic-api-key): `key === "WDSF_..."`,
#   environment variable NAMES in a mocked ConfigService.get.
# - 396822b docs/api/README.md (curl-auth-header): `Bearer your-access-token`
#   curl examples.
# - 396822b apps/backend/.env.example (private-key):
#   FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY="your-private-key" placeholder.
#
# Adding an entry: only for a reviewed false positive, with its reason above,
# copying the commit-pinned Fingerprint gitleaks prints. Prefer an inline
# `gitleaks:allow` comment for a one-off. A real secret is never baselined:
# remove it and revoke it (docs/exploitation/ci-cd-minimal.md).

